    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/SJ2JMVyz#npbOHMgi",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Each workhorse tool takes a required checkout, the directory that holds a board's vault, and the replay ledger counts the same arguments in another checkout as another call. A delegation to a checkout whose workhorse has no thread that can run turns starts it first; the other three tools refuse a checkout with no ready workhorse and say so. stop_workhorses names no checkout and no turn: it stops the whole work tree of every workhorse of the tab session, and says whether each stop is complete, partial or unconfirmed."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/SJ2JMVyz#glxfDGYq",
      "field": "responsibility",
      "value": "Delegate, steer, inspect, manage pending requests, and stop all work for the owned workhorse"
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/SJ2JMVyz#glxfDGYq",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "The coordinator's one door in, and each workhorse has its own. Its operations run one after another, so two coordinator effects never interleave on one thread, and each mutation is staged, settled and reported under an epoch operation. A delegation starts a turn on an idle workhorse and joins the queue of an active one Archboard created. An operation follows its workhorse turn to the end even after a voice start replaces the coordinator that asked for it; only the current coordinator may start one. Inspection reads actual turns, recent progress, descendants, and pending requests. Stop clears pending requests and interrupts the proven work tree. It observes settlement and reports complete, partial, or unconfirmed results. New work waits for resolution and a fresh user request. Existing ownership and epoch records govern effects."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/9ncuT5DP#2ffhMTdn",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Each change is checked against the queue it expected before and after the remote effect. Codex itself runs one turn at a time and takes the next queued message when a turn ends. Canonical ownership evidence admits the owned workhorse. Failed reads remain unavailable. Stop deletes pending requests instead of leaving the interrupted queue paused."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/SJ2JMVyz#mWD948LG",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "A workhorse works in its checkout, the directory that holds its vault, and its thread-link key is the tab session and the checkout together. It belongs to the checkout, not to the repository identity, so a new chosen checkout leaves it linked. A stop for the tab asks the operations of every workhorse to stop its whole work tree, and says what each stop came to. The coordinator's stop_workhorses tool stops every running workhorse of the tab by voice."
    },
